A||||16||GT Bastard||Challenged by the Duke...||||13||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||06-09-2000||10:37 PM||||A fellow Fiero nut and I were cruising 41st in my GT last night.  We pulled up a stop light, and next thing I hear is the sound of a toilet flushing.  So I look to my right, and sure enough, there's a guy in a torn-up t-shirt driving a red '84 SC with 17 or 18 inch chrome wheels.  The car(including the driver) was totally trashed aside from the wheels.  So anyhow, I couldn't resist the challenge.  When the light turned, he must have dropped the clutch because it actually chirped the tires.  So we were dead even from the start! Then of course I hit the gas...  Honestly, I hadn't expected my auto GT to pull away from him THAT quickly.  It was almost like he was standing still, even though I could hear that Iron Duke screaming in agony. The real kicker is, we caught up with that guy later that night in my friends '86SE V6 and he tried to race us again!  This time my friend stomped on it in second gear and once again, he was history... ||||reg||13
Z||000001||GT Bastard||06-11-2000||12:19 AM||||I guess it would be funnier if you had been there...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||06-11-2000||12:25 AM||||WOW!?! You really hate 4 bangger Fiero's huh?<BR>Many of your posts rip on the 4's. Im happy with my little 4 (so far) it runs perfect. I dont know why everyone hates them so much??||||reg||2
Z||000003||batboy||06-11-2000||12:38 AM||||Not only picking on a fellow Fiero, but a 2.5 ...that's low...LOL. Ok, I wasn't going to tell this story, but I blew away a nice black GT a while back while driving the Batmobile. I saw this sweet Fiero when we were going in opposite directions on the highway. It looked very clean. I whipped into a driveway and turned around to chase after him for a closer look and to maybe talk with him. I pulled up along side him in the oncoming lane (no traffic for miles) and looked it over as I paced him. He had a Holley side scoop and the car looked nice. I tried flagging him over. Maybe he thought I wanted to race or didn't like me running side by side on a two lane, because suddenly I heard him drop a gear and floor it. He pulled a car length while I was trying to figure out what was going on. I really didn't want to race a fellow Fiero, but of course he was clueless that I had a V8 in my notchback sleeper. I just wanted to chat. I finally said "screw it" and kicked the secondaries in, easily caught and passed him to show off my 2M8 lettering on the rear decklid. He sure looked surprised when I roared by him. I flashed my bat taillights three times, and begin gradually slowing. He slowed down too. I signalled and turned into a long wide driveway hoping he'd follow me in. He didn't. I turned around and went back the way I was originally headed. I feel so dirty and ashamed.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||06-11-2000||12:42 AM||||there, there, bat...thats ok im sure that we all understand..sometimes you just gotta do it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000005||GT Bastard||06-11-2000||01:42 AM||||Nice kill Batboy... Just to clarify, I don't "hate" the duke.  It's just that I've owned a couple and couldn't really develop an appreciation for that motor. No hard feelings.... ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shadow Wolf||06-11-2000||02:36 AM||||Well, it's good on gas.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Bolt a turbo on and wake the neighborhood.  I definately prefer my GT, but it was my friends '85 SC that got me started on Fieros.||||reg||4
Z||000007||batboy||06-11-2000||08:51 AM||||I miss having a 2.5 Fiero to commute in. One of these days I'm going to find a good 87 2.5 engine to replace the dead one in my 87 SE. I miss that 35 mpg on the highway.||||reg||1
Z||000008||phillip||06-11-2000||05:21 PM||||i've got 2 4cyl. fieros and i can't develope an appreciation for the engines in them.||||reg||1
Z||000009||My7Fieros||06-11-2000||06:01 PM||||When I was in 10th grade back in 88, I owned an 84 2m4. It was a fun car. I dont own any 4 bangers now, they're all 6's. But I do plan on buying one, like you said, GREAT gas milage!<BR>Lets not forget though, that the Fiero was originally a 4banger. Pontiac got the ok for it passing it off as a "commuter car", with obvious intentions in the future to make it a first class sports car.<BR>Ive got a friend who works at an automotive paint store who I buy all my paints from. He used to work for Pontiac during the 80's, and told me that Pontiac actually made a V8 Fiero (prototype obviously)...he said it was outperforming the Vette, and we all know GM can have that (for whatever reason). He also talked about how labor rates for repairs would triple when a Fiero came into the shop w/any kind of frame damage...very difficult to work on, helping in the demise of this wonderful car, but thats another topic.<BR>Anyway, no the 4 banger isnt gonna light up any asphault, but its still a fun car with super gas milage.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Patrick's Dad||06-11-2000||11:38 PM||||Yeah, I didn't feel too good about it when I did it, but....<P>I had just started working for a Pontiac dealer. The boss gave me reading material, then told me to read about a car, then grab a set of keys and drive a car, to get my own opinions. The last car I read up on ('cause I already knew a bit about it) was the Firebird. I hadn't driven anything with a stick (not even a Sunfire), so I grabbed a black Formula. I pulled out of the lot, jumped onto the highway (85mph just off the ramp. I laughed myself silly before I backed off so as not to get a ticket) and headed for Quincy (Pronounced KWIN-zee here in MA, like John Quincy Adams, not Kwin-SEE, like Quincy Magoo). <P>I took the back roads back to Weymouth, and, on Quicy Ave, stopped right next to a black GT. "Self," I said to myself, "you're going to hate yourself for this, but..."<P>"I understand." I answered as I dropped the clutch.<P>He was so overmatched by the LT-1 that I still feel bad. But I still tell the story.||||reg||11
